217
00:16:15,619 --> 00:16:19,090
- Someone's helped me
understand the real you.
- Someone?

218
00:16:19,357 --> 00:16:23,327
Your ruthless ambition,
your private self-loathing...

219
00:16:23,594 --> 00:16:26,231
and that lost and lonely
little girl inside.

220
00:16:26,464 --> 00:16:28,233
Lost and lonely what?

221
00:16:28,433 --> 00:16:31,470
You heard me.
Thanks, Dewey, I'll return it.

222
00:16:31,703 --> 00:16:33,939
Lost and lonely what?

223
00:16:34,173 --> 00:16:37,543
- Little girl inside.
- I thought you were
supposed to be in Woodsboro.

224
00:16:37,776 --> 00:16:39,946
Well, I'm surprised
you thought about me at all.

225
00:16:40,179 --> 00:16:44,016
Listen, I gotta get back to work.
I really don't have time for this.

226
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:46,319
- Wait a minute. You work here?
- Yeah.

227
00:16:46,586 --> 00:16:48,155
The movie needed
a technical advisor.

228
00:16:48,422 --> 00:16:50,857
Someone who went through the real
experience, knew the real people.

229
00:16:51,058 --> 00:16:54,195
- Hey, Dewey.
- Hey, Tom.

230
00:16:54,428 --> 00:16:57,231
Hey! It's the real Gale Weathers.

231
00:16:57,465 --> 00:16:59,434
Real from top to bottom.

232
00:16:59,701 --> 00:17:01,703
Tom Prinze.
Watch your show all the time.

233
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:06,074
You're so right. Pop culture
is the politics ofthe 21 st century.

234
00:17:06,341 --> 00:17:07,977
- Thank you.
- And that story that you did...

235
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:10,345
last month on me crashing my car?

236
00:17:10,579 --> 00:17:13,583
-Wow, was that ever powerful journalism.
-Right, uh--

237
00:17:13,816 --> 00:17:16,919
I especially liked the way
you implied that it was caused
by drinking and drugs.

238
00:17:17,153 --> 00:17:19,923
And that the tyre blowout was faked.
That was great.

239
00:17:20,156 --> 00:17:22,025
Tom, sometimes in journalism
you have to--

240
00:17:22,259 --> 00:17:24,594
Are you parked in the lot?
'Cause I should check to make sure...

241
00:17:24,828 --> 00:17:29,332
that nobody's messed
with your brake line.

242
00:17:29,599 --> 00:17:33,938
Who's he supposed to be?

243
00:17:35,006 --> 00:17:38,777
He's playing you? Him?

244
00:17:38,977 --> 00:17:40,946
What?

245
00:17:41,246 --> 00:17:43,314
I did not come here
to fight with you, Dewey.

246
00:17:43,548 --> 00:17:46,385
- Cotton's killer left a picture.
- Of Sid's mom.

247
00:17:46,585 --> 00:17:49,221
- The detectives told me.
- Well, does Sidney know about it?

248
00:17:49,421 --> 00:17:51,991
Listen, Sidney doesn't need
you and your camera in her life.

249
00:17:52,191 --> 00:17:55,529
Do you see a camera?

250
00:17:56,829 --> 00:17:58,832
Right. You bought me
this purse, didn't you?

251
00:17:59,099 --> 00:18:00,834
- Yeah.
- Look, it's-it's a habit.

252
00:18:01,101 --> 00:18:02,836
-I-I walk outta the house, I turn it on.
-What the hell is this?

253
00:18:03,069 --> 00:18:04,538
- It's like perfume.
- Gale Weathers?

254
00:18:04,838 --> 00:18:07,074
- Could I be more popular?
- No press.

255
00:18:07,275 --> 00:18:09,677
Mo press on set.
Get that woman outta here.

256
00:18:09,910 --> 00:18:12,914
- Yes, Mr Milton. Let's go.
- Wait a minute. Wait a minute.
Where is Detective Kincaid?

257
00:18:13,181 --> 00:18:14,916
- I am working with Kincaid, Dewey.
- Come on. Move along, miss. Let's go.

258
00:18:15,183 --> 00:18:21,991
Rules are rules, Gale.
But, really, it was great seeing you.

259
00:18:22,591 --> 00:18:25,728
<i>Stab 3 is a closed set. But just up
ahead is the old Seinfeld stage.</i>

260
00:18:25,961 --> 00:18:27,931
Now, does anybody
need a potty break?

261
00:18:28,164 --> 00:18:30,366
- Oh, I do.
- Yeah, me too.

262
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:34,071
Okay, let go!
Thanks for your help, boys.

263
00:18:34,304 --> 00:18:38,041
Holy shit, Silent Bob. It's that
TV news chick, Connie-fuckin'-Chung!

264
00:18:38,241 --> 00:18:41,312
Hey, Connie, how's Maury?

265
00:18:41,612 --> 00:18:46,951
Dude, I think she likes me.
See how she's lookin' at me?

266
00:18:47,886 --> 00:18:50,288
<i>It's happening again.</i>

267
00:18:50,488 --> 00:18:52,824
Cotton had a lot
of enemies, Sid.

268
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:56,661
The police aren't saying
it's related to us.

269
00:18:57,395 --> 00:19:00,766
Do you ever think about her?

270
00:19:01,634 --> 00:19:03,102
Your mom?

271
00:19:03,369 --> 00:19:06,306
None of this would've
ever happened if she hadn't--

272
00:19:06,506 --> 00:19:09,909
if she hadn't--

273
00:19:12,212 --> 00:19:14,315
Why'd she have
so many secrets, Dad?

274
00:19:14,615 --> 00:19:18,519
Listen, maybe it's time
you came home.

275
00:19:19,053 --> 00:19:22,157
I'm worried about you, kid. Out here
by yourself. You never see anyone.

276
00:19:22,389 --> 00:19:25,960
The only people you talk to
don't even know your real name.

277
00:19:26,161 --> 00:19:29,731
It's as if you don't exist.

278
00:19:31,166 --> 00:19:37,039
That's the idea. Psychos
can't kill what they can't find.

279
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:53,923
Sid, come here.

280
00:20:54,157 --> 00:20:56,692
Mother needs to talk to you.

281
00:20:56,926 --> 00:21:00,330
Everything you touch, Sid, dies!

282
00:21:00,564 --> 00:21:04,134
You're poison.
You're just like me.

283
00:21:04,368 --> 00:21:08,106
You're just like me.

284
00:21:08,339 --> 00:21:13,945
Oh, my God!
What have they done to me?

285
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,681
They'll do it to you.

286
00:21:16,981 --> 00:21:20,619
- They'll do it to you, baby.
- Mom?

287
00:22:07,804 --> 00:22:11,140
Roman?

288
00:22:12,208 --> 00:22:17,047
<i>Stab 3.
Jesus, I gotta get a new agent.</i>

289
00:22:17,848 --> 00:22:21,219
Roman?

290
00:22:28,226 --> 00:22:31,563
Someone here?

291
00:22:38,337 --> 00:22:40,173
Stan, my man.
He does good work, huh?

292
00:22:40,406 --> 00:22:42,175
- Thank you. Thank you very much.
- Fuck you very much.

293
00:22:42,409 --> 00:22:46,146
- Tyson, go to hell.
- Well, excuse us, Sarah. Makeup tests.

294
00:22:46,413 --> 00:22:49,083
Yeah, makeup. You can use it.
Damn it, have you seen Roman?

295
00:22:49,349 --> 00:22:51,618
Look, everyone in the office
has gone home already.

296
00:22:51,852 --> 00:22:56,523
- He said it was important.
- Everything's important to Roman.

297
00:23:18,648 --> 00:23:22,019
Oh, shit!

298
00:23:28,993 --> 00:23:31,195
<i>- Director's office.
- Sarah, it's Roman.</i>

299
00:23:31,428 --> 00:23:34,232
<i>I'm sorry I'm running late. I'm still
on the 405. I'm about ten minutes away.</i>

300
00:23:34,499 --> 00:23:38,736
Oh, it's no problem. I'm just
lookin' at your music video awards.

301
00:23:38,970 --> 00:23:42,241
<i>Since I got you on thephone, let's--
let's talk about your character, okay?</i>

302
00:23:42,474 --> 00:23:45,344
What character? I'm Candy,
the chick who gets killed second.

303
00:23:45,577 --> 00:23:48,614
<i>- I'm only in two scenes.
- You're not happy with your part.</i>

304
00:23:48,881 --> 00:23:52,551
I'm not happy that I am
35 playing a 21-year-old.

305
00:23:52,785 --> 00:23:54,654
I'm not happy
that I have to die naked.

306
00:23:54,921 --> 00:23:57,623
And I'm not happy that my character is
too stupid to have a gun in the house...

307
00:23:57,857 --> 00:24:00,594
after her boyfriend's
been cut into fish sticks.

308
00:24:00,827 --> 00:24:03,930
<i>Great, okay.
So let's--let's run the lines.</i>

309
00:24:04,197 --> 00:24:05,732
Fine.

310
00:24:05,999 --> 00:24:10,304
<i>Page28.
Candy's big moment.</i>

311
00:24:11,706 --> 00:24:14,476
Page 28.

312
00:24:14,709 --> 00:24:16,944
Ring-ring.
Hello?

313
00:24:17,178 --> 00:24:19,548
<i>- Hello?
- Who's this?</i>

314
00:24:19,781 --> 00:24:21,750
<i>- Who's this?
- This is Candy.</i>

315
00:24:21,984 --> 00:24:23,785
Hang on.
Let me get some clothes.

316
00:24:24,019 --> 00:24:26,789
See? I don't understand why I have
to start the scene in the shower.

317
00:24:27,023 --> 00:24:30,359
<i>The whole shower thing's been done.
Vertigo. Hello?</i>

318
00:24:30,593 --> 00:24:34,664
And I mean, my boyfriend just died.
Why am I showering?

319
00:24:34,965 --> 00:24:36,900
<i>Why don't we just read the scene?</i>

320
00:24:37,133 --> 00:24:41,906
<i>Candy. Nice name. Is that like
Candy Cane or Candy Apple?</i>

321
00:24:42,139 --> 00:24:44,341
Whatever.

322
00:24:44,575 --> 00:24:46,644
Come on.
Who is this?

323
00:24:46,878 --> 00:24:48,947
I think you have
the wrong number.

324
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:52,550
<i>- But you know my favourite name?
- I'm hanging up right now.</i>

325
00:24:52,784 --> 00:24:54,553
<i>It's Sarah.</i>

326
00:24:54,786 --> 00:24:57,923
Roman, that's not the line.

327
00:24:58,156 --> 00:25:00,459
<i>It is in my script.</i>

328
00:25:00,726 --> 00:25:03,395
Has there been another goddam rewrite?
How the fuck...

329
00:25:03,629 --> 00:25:06,399
are we supposed to learn our lines when
there's a new script every 15 minutes?

330
00:25:06,632 --> 00:25:10,303
<i>It's not just a new script.
It's a new movie.</i>

331
00:25:10,503 --> 00:25:13,707
<i>- What? What movie?
- My movie.</i>

332
00:25:13,941 --> 00:25:18,846
<i>And it's called Sarah Gets
Skewered Like a Fuckin' Pig!</i>

333
00:25:19,079 --> 00:25:23,984
<i>Still in character, Sarah?</i>

334
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:41,771
Shit.

335
00:26:02,927 --> 00:26:04,996
<i>Thank you for calling
Sunrise Picture Studios.</i>

336
00:26:05,263 --> 00:26:08,767
<i>If you'd like today's
commissary menu, press one.</i>

337
00:26:10,635 --> 00:26:14,040
Mr Bridger?

338
00:26:26,853 --> 00:26:29,389
<i>If you'd like to hear previews of
upcoming Sunrise Pictures'releases...</i>

339
00:26:29,623 --> 00:26:30,757
<i>press four.</i>

340
00:26:30,991 --> 00:26:32,893
<i>If you'd like information about
Sunrise Pictures' merchandise...</i>

341
00:26:33,127 --> 00:26:35,964
<i>- Come on. Come on.
- press five.</i>

342
00:26:36,163 --> 00:26:41,670
<i>If you're trying to reach Lot Security
or you have an emergency, press six.</i>

343
00:26:49,611 --> 00:26:52,148
Shit!

344
00:26:57,487 --> 00:27:01,391
Oh! Fuck!

345
00:27:16,107 --> 00:27:18,376
Look, I wanna get something straight.

346
00:27:18,610 --> 00:27:23,048
I only got into this because
the police asked for my help.

347
00:27:23,214 --> 00:27:25,150
- Why would the police come to you?
- Well, I did write..

348
00:27:25,451 --> 00:27:27,353
the definitive book
on the Woodsboro murders.

349
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:30,289
I'm sure you just can't wait
to write another one.

350
00:27:30,523 --> 00:27:32,959
- What about you?
- What about me?

351
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:37,564
You said you'd never leave Woodsboro.
"It's the only place that's real."

352
00:27:37,797 --> 00:27:41,735
But now you're here.
Not with me.

353
00:27:42,436 --> 00:27:44,204
Dewey, I took care ofyou.

354
00:27:44,438 --> 00:27:46,874
I waited until you were well,
but I couldn't stay there.

355
00:27:47,175 --> 00:27:50,111
It was like dog years. One year in
Woodsboro is like seven anywhere else.

356
00:27:50,311 --> 00:27:54,983
So it's off to Paris for a week?
New York for a month? L.A. forever?

357
00:27:55,184 --> 00:27:57,719
It was fucking 60 Minutes II.

358
00:27:57,919 --> 00:27:59,721
- I couldn't say no. I could've
been the next Diane Sawyer.
- Wait a minute.

359
00:27:59,922 --> 00:28:04,960
What's wrong with just being
Gale Weathers? I liked her.

360
00:28:07,130 --> 00:28:09,432
It didn't work, Dewey.
We tried. We're different.

361
00:28:09,732 --> 00:28:13,203
You used to say
that was our strength.

362
00:28:15,039 --> 00:28:18,542
- Well--
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

363
00:28:18,842 --> 00:28:22,480
Dewey, you're not just here because
of that second-rate K-Mart...

364
00:28:22,714 --> 00:28:24,482
straight-to-video
version of me, are you?

365
00:28:24,782 --> 00:28:30,889
Brace yourself, Gale.
All of this is actually not about you.

366
00:28:31,556 --> 00:28:35,961
All of what, Dewey?
You do know something, don't you?

367
00:28:36,528 --> 00:28:38,998
- Off the record?
- Always.

368
00:28:39,198 --> 00:28:41,868
Two months ago, the Woodsboro police
got a call from a woman...

369
00:28:42,068 --> 00:28:43,836
who said she was with Stab 3.

370
00:28:44,036 --> 00:28:46,573
She wanted to see the file
on Sid, "for research."

371
00:28:46,773 --> 00:28:48,575
- And?
- The boys said no.

372
00:28:48,775 --> 00:28:50,543
And she wouldn't give her name.

373
00:28:50,777 --> 00:28:53,213
A month later,
the station gets broken into.

374
00:28:53,414 --> 00:28:56,183
- The file room gets ransacked.
- And someone stole Sid's file?

375
00:28:56,416 --> 00:28:59,820
I already removed it.

376
00:29:00,021 --> 00:29:03,090
I think someone on the film
is tryin' to find Sid.

377
00:29:03,357 --> 00:29:07,930
- I'm sorry, this is incredible.
- I said, "off the record."

378
00:29:08,497 --> 00:29:11,400
Right.

379
00:29:13,369 --> 00:29:15,004
It's Jennifer.
She needs me.

380
00:29:15,271 --> 00:29:17,573
-Jennifer?
- Gotta run.

381
00:29:17,773 --> 00:29:21,511
- Wait! Dewey, where are you going?
- I'm on duty.

382
00:29:34,225 --> 00:29:36,160
Stop following me.

383
00:29:36,460 --> 00:29:39,430
I happen to be working
for the police, damn it!

384
00:29:39,631 --> 00:29:42,967
- You're not a detective, Gale.
- Neither are you, Mr Incognito.

385
00:29:43,167 --> 00:29:46,905
- Uh, you left your motor running.
- Damn it.

386
00:29:47,106 --> 00:29:51,243
Fans, I can handle. Fans, they want
a picture, they want a conversation.

387
00:29:51,543 --> 00:29:53,646
I can handle fans!
You see this, Dewey?

388
00:29:53,913 --> 00:29:57,416
I haven't had one ofthese in a year and
a half. Someone's gonna pay for this.

389
00:29:57,650 --> 00:30:01,188
-Jennifer, settle down. What happened?
- I'm with him.
- You.

390
00:30:01,421 --> 00:30:03,723
Like I'm ever going
to win an award playing you.

391
00:30:03,923 --> 00:30:06,827
- There's been a second murder.
- Who?

392
00:30:07,061 --> 00:30:08,830
- Sarah Darling.
- Where?

393
00:30:09,063 --> 00:30:11,332
-At the studio.
-Where? Nancy Drew
wants to know where.

394
00:30:11,532 --> 00:30:14,469
Cotton Weary. Sarah Darling.
Don't you get it?

395
00:30:14,702 --> 00:30:19,140
Someone's killing them in the order
they die in the movie.

396
00:30:19,975 --> 00:30:24,646
- Dewey, who gets killed third?
- Who gets killed third?

397
00:30:28,584 --> 00:30:32,054
You do.

398
00:30:40,297 --> 00:30:43,066
I get killed in Stab 3?
I get killed?

399
00:30:43,333 --> 00:30:45,769
- Yeah.
- Dewey, where are you going?

400
00:30:46,070 --> 00:30:48,306
I have to get something
from my trailer.

401
00:30:48,540 --> 00:30:51,375
Your--
You live here with her?

402
00:30:51,609 --> 00:30:54,212
- Yeah.
- Oh, my God!

403
00:30:54,479 --> 00:30:56,781
I needed a place to stay,
and she said she liked having me around.

404
00:30:57,015 --> 00:31:00,786
- Why?
- She says I make her feel safe.

405
00:31:01,020 --> 00:31:03,789
- She says I'm her rock.
- Her rock?

406
00:31:04,056 --> 00:31:06,592
Yeah. If you weren't so concerned
with pretensions and appearances...

407
00:31:06,859 --> 00:31:09,496
you'd be able to appreciate the
positivity and emotional centeredness...

408
00:31:09,728 --> 00:31:13,466
I provide a woman.

409
00:31:14,701 --> 00:31:17,470
Stone, I'm headed
to the crime scene.

410
00:31:17,704 --> 00:31:23,010
You stay by Jennifer's side.
I suggest a search of the grounds.

411
00:31:23,277 --> 00:31:26,381
Hey, Dewdrop.
Can I have a word?

412
00:31:26,614 --> 00:31:30,418
Just so it can be straight. I'm
the professional celebrity guard here.

413
00:31:30,651 --> 00:31:33,188
My resume lists Julia Roberts,
Salmon Rushdie, Posh Spice.

414
00:31:33,388 --> 00:31:36,058
You are the Hollywood hanger-oner.

415
00:31:36,291 --> 00:31:38,360
'Cause you're just no good
as a cop any more.

416
00:31:38,594 --> 00:31:40,262
Your resume reads
like the obituaries.

417
00:31:40,496 --> 00:31:43,065
So how about you take suggestions
from me? All right?

418
00:31:43,299 --> 00:31:46,669
Whatever you say.

419
00:31:47,037 --> 00:31:49,373
Hmm. Same deal?
Found with the body?

420
00:31:49,639 --> 00:31:52,709
- Yeah, Maureen Prescott again.
- This is great.

421
00:31:52,943 --> 00:31:55,346
Ten more murders
and we can publish a calendar.

422
00:31:55,579 --> 00:31:57,347
The old "killer playing
with the cops" routine.

423
00:31:57,581 --> 00:32:01,119
Very Hannibal Lecter.
Very Seven.

424
00:32:01,352 --> 00:32:03,721
Doesn't the killer come after
the cops in those movies?

425
00:32:03,955 --> 00:32:05,723
Usually one cop makes it.

426
00:32:05,957 --> 00:32:09,894
- And?
- One cop doesn't.

427
00:32:10,161 --> 00:32:11,897
- Usually.
- Detective Kincaid.

428
00:32:12,164 --> 00:32:14,433
- What do we know? Same killer?
- Hey, hey.

429
00:32:14,667 --> 00:32:17,670
<i>Terminal Entertainment,
this is a crime scene, okay?</i>

430
00:32:17,903 --> 00:32:19,872
Wallace, Miss Weathers
is working with me now.

431
00:32:20,106 --> 00:32:21,741
- Thank you, Detective.
- You're welcome.

432
00:32:22,008 --> 00:32:25,445
Well, in that case, I'm gonna go dust
for fingerprints with Jane Pauley.

433
00:32:25,679 --> 00:32:29,350
Uh, photos, Wallace, please?
Thank you.

434
00:32:29,582 --> 00:32:32,319
New pictures, same person.
Anything turn up on your research yet?

435
00:32:32,553 --> 00:32:35,790
- Nothing that will help with these.
- What about an increased
police presence around Jennifer?

436
00:32:36,024 --> 00:32:39,394
- She's the next one
to get killed in the script.
- She has a bodyguard.

437
00:32:39,627 --> 00:32:42,364
And besides, the producers told us
that there were three different
versions of the script.

438
00:32:42,598 --> 00:32:45,000
Something about trying to keep
the ending off the Internet.
You should know that.

439
00:32:45,233 --> 00:32:47,903
You're the technical advisor, right?

440
00:32:48,170 --> 00:32:50,806
Three versions.
Three different characters die next.

441
00:32:51,039 --> 00:32:53,142
And we don't know which one
the killer read.

442
00:32:53,409 --> 00:32:56,679
Hey, hold up.

443
00:32:57,279 --> 00:33:00,517
<i>All I ever wanted to do
was make a real classic lovestory.</i>

444
00:33:00,717 --> 00:33:03,353
And the studio said they'd let me.
I just had to do
a scary movie for them first.

445
00:33:03,553 --> 00:33:05,622
And now we're shut down,
and I am fucked!

446
00:33:05,889 --> 00:33:07,892
God, it's not the end
of the world, Roman.

447
00:33:08,125 --> 00:33:11,929
That is so easy foryou to say. You can
always go back to, to MustSee TV.

448
00:33:12,163 --> 00:33:16,400
You know, I have no movie,
I'm about to turn 30, and it
looks like I'm now the next target.

449
00:33:16,634 --> 00:33:20,005
- What?
- You? Why you?

450
00:33:20,105 --> 00:33:22,174
Do you think this wasn't a message?

451
00:33:22,341 --> 00:33:24,743
- Roman Bridger?
- What?

452
00:33:25,010 --> 00:33:26,812
Mr Bridger,
you didn't tell us...

453
00:33:27,046 --> 00:33:29,148
you spoke with Sarah Darling
before she was murdered.

454
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:30,950
Uh, spoke with her, uh, when?

455
00:33:31,183 --> 00:33:34,154
The guard said she was here
for a meeting with you.

456
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:36,622
- What meeting? I don't--
- We talked with her roommate too.

457
00:33:36,889 --> 00:33:39,593
Says you called Sarah,
told her to come down to the studio.

458
00:33:39,826 --> 00:33:41,595
- Roommate answered the phone.
Says it was you.
- Wait a minute. No, no.

459
00:33:41,829 --> 00:33:43,597
I-I never called her.
I never told her to go anywhere.

460
00:33:43,830 --> 00:33:45,632
Roommate says she knows
your voice, Mr Bridger.

461
00:33:45,833 --> 00:33:49,970
Well, she wasn't speaking with me! God!
Look, I did not call Sarah Darling.

462
00:33:50,204 --> 00:33:53,174
- Sarah Darling said you did.
- Someone's trying to ruin my movie.

463
00:33:53,374 --> 00:33:55,010
Someone wants to kill
my movie!

464
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:57,512
All right, we'll talk about
your movie down at the station.

465
00:33:57,746 --> 00:34:00,549
- All right.
- This is the scene
where you come with us.

466
00:34:00,816 --> 00:34:03,752
Dewey,Jennifer--
Wait a minute.

467
00:34:04,052 --> 00:34:06,756
She wasn't talking with me
on the phone. I'm coming!

468
00:34:06,989 --> 00:34:11,594
I'll call him in. Battery. Mr Riley,
do you have a cell phone I can borrow?

469
00:34:11,828 --> 00:34:14,998
Yeah.

470
00:34:15,299 --> 00:34:17,834
- Thank you.
- God. Roman.

471
00:34:18,135 --> 00:34:20,604
Remind me not
to sleep with him again.

472
00:34:20,805 --> 00:34:24,208
Come here, Cherokee.

473
00:34:25,376 --> 00:34:27,712
California Women's Crisis Counseling.
My name is Laura. How can I help you?

474
00:34:27,979 --> 00:34:31,716
<i>Oh, Laura.
I do have a crisis.</i>

475
00:34:31,916 --> 00:34:34,453
Okay, well, whatever it is,
you can tell me.

476
00:34:34,686 --> 00:34:39,058
<i>Oh, my God.
I've killed someone, Laura.</i>

477
00:34:39,158 --> 00:34:41,060
<i>- Are you sure ?
- Uh-huh, I'm sure.</i>

478
00:34:41,294 --> 00:34:44,163
<i>I killed someone, I know it!
Oh, my God.</i>

479
00:34:44,396 --> 00:34:46,733
<i>- Well, then, um--
- I did.</i>

480
00:34:46,966 --> 00:34:48,702
Then the people you need to call
are the police.

481
00:34:48,902 --> 00:34:53,040
<i>No, I need to call you!
Just you.</i>

482
00:34:53,273 --> 00:34:55,042
I'm sorry, your-your voice--

483
00:34:55,276 --> 00:35:00,414
<i>Don't you wanna know
how you can help, Laura?</i>

484
00:35:03,450 --> 00:35:05,820
<i>Are you listening to me?
Huh?</i>

485
00:35:06,054 --> 00:35:09,158
<i>- Who is this?
- It's Mother, Laura.</i>

486
00:35:09,391 --> 00:35:12,861
<i>Now, be a good girl
and turn on the news.</i>

487
00:35:13,095 --> 00:35:16,531
<i>Do as Mother tells you!</i>

488
00:35:16,765 --> 00:35:19,402
You're not my mother. How did you
get this number? Who is this?

489
00:35:19,635 --> 00:35:22,305
<i>You know your mother's voice
when you hear it!</i>

490
00:35:22,539 --> 00:35:26,610
<i>Now, turn on the news!</i>

491
00:35:28,245 --> 00:35:30,213
<i>And with a second cast member
murdered, Stab 3...</i>

492
00:35:30,413 --> 00:35:32,916
<i>has been officially shut down,
prompting those involved...</i>

493
00:35:33,117 --> 00:35:35,186
<i>to hope and pray that
these killings maybe over.</i>

494
00:35:35,453 --> 00:35:37,054
<i>Just one question.</i>

495
00:35:37,321 --> 00:35:42,260
<i>Do you think it's over, Sidney?
Do you?</i>

496
00:36:04,818 --> 00:36:08,656
<i>The sky was dark this morning</i>

497
00:36:09,657 --> 00:36:13,160
<i>Not a bird in a tree</i>

498
00:36:19,934 --> 00:36:21,737
Is this a wrap party
or is this a wrap party?

499
00:36:21,937 --> 00:36:25,607
Scene 34.
"Maureen's Murder Flashback."

500
00:36:25,807 --> 00:36:29,445
- I never liked that scene.
- That's 'cause you weren't in it.

501
00:36:29,679 --> 00:36:31,480
Scenes 40 through 47.

502
00:36:31,747 --> 00:36:36,253
- "The Prescott House Flashbacks."
- Tom, stop it.

503
00:36:36,485 --> 00:36:38,221
You're scaring me.
Two people are dead.

504
00:36:38,488 --> 00:36:40,524
Scaring you?

505
00:36:40,724 --> 00:36:43,927
Give the sweet,
young ingenue act a rest.

506
00:36:44,227 --> 00:36:48,533
- You're drunk.
- I'm coping.

507
00:36:49,667 --> 00:36:52,937
I bet she fought and clawed
for that Sidney part.

508
00:36:53,137 --> 00:36:55,674
I bet she stepped on any poor girl
that got in her way.

509
00:36:55,841 --> 00:36:59,911
- So you asked her out and she said no?
- That has nothing to do with it.

510
00:37:00,178 --> 00:37:02,381
Right.
Come on, Dewey.

511
00:37:02,581 --> 00:37:04,683
Scene 50.

512
00:37:04,983 --> 00:37:08,888
"Dewey Saves the Day."

513
00:37:36,484 --> 00:37:38,253
She's so focused on success
that she never thinks...

514
00:37:38,487 --> 00:37:40,256
about who she's hurting
to get it.

515
00:37:40,489 --> 00:37:42,392
And you saved her life, like,
how many times?

516
00:37:42,659 --> 00:37:44,393
Gale wants the whole world
to love her.

517
00:37:44,660 --> 00:37:47,197
One person's never enough.
She's a dreamer.

518
00:37:47,464 --> 00:37:50,500
-No, she's a narcissistic, psycho bitch.
-No, she's not.

519
00:37:50,733 --> 00:37:52,702
She's got a good heart.
She does.

520
00:37:52,969 --> 00:37:59,009
She just hides it away because
she thinks people see that as weak.

521
00:37:59,710 --> 00:38:02,580
This is a good picture of you.
You look just like her.

522
00:38:02,814 --> 00:38:04,916
God, Dewey.

523
00:38:05,183 --> 00:38:08,120
You make it sound like
you're still in love with her.

524
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:10,088
And I left out the part
that she's cruel...

525
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:16,062
and selfish,
obsessive and annoying.

526
00:38:16,495 --> 00:38:19,198
We have one Gale Weathers here.
We don't need two.

527
00:38:19,465 --> 00:38:24,237
Hey, Dewdrop,
got your girlfriend out here.

528
00:38:26,106 --> 00:38:29,276
Look who I found slinkin'
around the yard. The nightly news.

529
00:38:29,510 --> 00:38:31,344
I wasn't slinking.
I was walking.

530
00:38:31,611 --> 00:38:33,881
You were eaves dropping
at the bedroom window.

531
00:38:34,114 --> 00:38:36,583
Yeah, a bedroom that
you seemed awfully at home in.

532
00:38:36,817 --> 00:38:39,353
All right, let's talk.

533
00:38:39,587 --> 00:38:42,457
Come on.

534
00:38:42,691 --> 00:38:45,360
- What's this about, Gale?
- Did you know they released Roman?

535
00:38:45,593 --> 00:38:47,262
Sarah's call didn't come
from his cell phone.

536
00:38:47,496 --> 00:38:51,033
- Where did it come from then?
- A cloned cell phone. It's untraceable.

537
00:38:51,266 --> 00:38:53,669
Well, thanks for the update, Gale.
Why don't you just go back home?

538
00:38:53,903 --> 00:38:57,973
Dewey, wait a minute.
Just wait one second.

539
00:38:58,441 --> 00:39:00,677
How old do you think
Maureen Prescott is in this picture?

540
00:39:00,910 --> 00:39:03,312
- Nineteen, twenty.
- That's what I thought,
so I checked it out.

541
00:39:03,546 --> 00:39:06,884
I cannot find any information about
her at this age. I mean, nothing.

542
00:39:07,117 --> 00:39:10,554
She lived in Woodsboro her whole life.
Someone there must know something.

543
00:39:10,787 --> 00:39:13,057
Almost her whole life.
Two years before...

544
00:39:13,257 --> 00:39:15,627
she met Sidney's father,
she left Woodsboro.

545
00:39:15,894 --> 00:39:18,196
No one has any idea
where she went or what she did.

546
00:39:18,429 --> 00:39:22,501
I mean, it's-it's like she fell into
a black hole, Dewey! She vanished!

547
00:39:22,701 --> 00:39:24,469
- So?
- So?

548
00:39:24,703 --> 00:39:27,239
Why is the killer
leaving pictures of-of Maureen?

549
00:39:27,439 --> 00:39:31,944
And why these pictures at-at--
at that point in her life?

550
00:39:32,111 --> 00:39:35,115
I don't know! If I thought
like a homicidal maniac...

551
00:39:35,348 --> 00:39:38,952
then I'd know how
a homicidal maniac thinks.

552
00:39:43,023 --> 00:39:44,725
What?

553
00:39:44,958 --> 00:39:49,197
-Jennifer.
-Jennifer?

554
00:39:52,633 --> 00:39:55,437
Look at the buildings.
The second story. There and there.

555
00:39:55,670 --> 00:39:58,473
It's the same!
It's the same street 28 years ago.

556
00:39:58,707 --> 00:40:02,945
Oh, my God. Maureen Prescott was
at the back lot at Sunrise Studios!

557
00:40:03,179 --> 00:40:06,716
- Oh, my God.
- I gotta make some calls.

558
00:40:19,029 --> 00:40:20,798
Steven Stone
Protection Services.

559
00:40:21,031 --> 00:40:22,800
<i>Stone, where are you?</i>

560
00:40:23,034 --> 00:40:25,469
I'm just checking
your tin can, Dewdrop.

561
00:40:25,703 --> 00:40:27,405
<i>Well, come back inside
and stay with Jennifer.</i>

562
00:40:27,639 --> 00:40:29,641
<i>Something's happened.
I have to go to the police.</i>

563
00:40:29,875 --> 00:40:33,879
Is that an order, Dewdrop? 'Cause
Steven Stone doesn't work for you.

564
00:40:34,112 --> 00:40:38,550
<i>Get back in the house, Stone.
Would I call you if it wasn 't important?</i>

565
00:40:38,784 --> 00:40:40,686
<i>- What are you doing in there anyway?
- Me?</i>

566
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,089
I'm just checking to make sure
there's no killer in here...

567
00:40:43,322 --> 00:40:45,892
waitin' to off you
like he did your little sister.

568
00:40:46,125 --> 00:40:48,929
<i>What did you say?
I can't believe you said that.</i>

569
00:40:49,162 --> 00:40:51,264
<i>That makes me...</i>

570
00:40:51,531 --> 00:40:55,035
angry!

571
00:40:55,269 --> 00:40:58,171
Fucker!

572
00:41:09,351 --> 00:41:12,721
Gotta call Kincaid.

573
00:41:17,092 --> 00:41:21,598
Dewey, where is everybody?

574
00:41:26,202 --> 00:41:28,839
- Oh, God.
-Jennifer?

575
00:41:29,072 --> 00:41:32,376
Angelina?
Tom?

576
00:41:32,643 --> 00:41:36,914
Oh, my God!
What happened?

577
00:41:38,415 --> 00:41:42,454
Don't do that.
I'm overreacting.

578
00:41:42,888 --> 00:41:46,324
Dewdrop?

579
00:41:50,295 --> 00:41:54,700
- Stone?
- Oh, my God!

580
00:41:55,401 --> 00:41:57,169
Oh, God, Stone!

581
00:41:57,403 --> 00:42:00,540
Oh, God!

582
00:42:03,509 --> 00:42:08,716
- Dewey, is he dead?
- Yeah.

583
00:42:09,283 --> 00:42:12,853
Everyone back inside!

584
00:42:15,056 --> 00:42:18,459
It's all right.
Don't panic.

585
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:22,731
Okay, outside. Everyone,
stay together and try to remain calm.

586
00:42:22,965 --> 00:42:24,733
A phone!

587
00:42:24,966 --> 00:42:27,236
- It's not mine.
- It's not mine.

588
00:42:27,503 --> 00:42:31,006
Shit!
It's the fax.

589
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:40,183
"Interior, Jennifer's house. Living
room, night." It's a script page.

590
00:42:40,450 --> 00:42:44,154
- W-W-What's it say?
- "With the bodyguard stabbed to death,
the five stand trapped.

591
00:42:44,421 --> 00:42:46,523
- He's rewriting the movie.
- As the killer waits outside...

592
00:42:46,724 --> 00:42:48,626
suddenly the fax machine
sends news of their fates."

593
00:42:48,893 --> 00:42:50,661
It's a trick!
Everybody, outside!

594
00:42:50,928 --> 00:42:52,930
- Outside where he can
pick us off one by one?
- Shut up!

595
00:42:53,164 --> 00:42:55,100
"The killer prepares to grant
mercy to only one of them."

596
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:58,369
Don't you get it? The killer says he's
outside because he wants us here inside.

597
00:42:58,603 --> 00:43:00,639
- Which one is it?
- Come on!

598
00:43:00,839 --> 00:43:02,775
"Who will survive? Is it Jennifer?
Tom? Angelina? Dewey? Gale?

599
00:43:03,042 --> 00:43:06,412
- The killer will give mercy to--"
- Everyone outside!

600
00:43:06,645 --> 00:43:09,716
He grants mercy to who?
I wanna know what happens!

601
00:43:09,983 --> 00:43:12,418
- I wanna know what happens!
- Wait for the fucking movie!

602
00:43:12,652 --> 00:43:14,421
- I've gotta know! I'm goin' back in!
- No.

603
00:43:14,654 --> 00:43:16,956
All right, everyone, back.
Stay together.

604
00:43:17,257 --> 00:43:19,226
- What's it say?
- "And the...

605
00:43:19,459 --> 00:43:21,362
killer will give mercy to...

606
00:43:21,562 --> 00:43:23,997
- whoever--"
- Whoever?

607
00:43:24,264 --> 00:43:26,534
Whoever?

608
00:43:26,767 --> 00:43:28,303
Piece of shit.

609
00:43:28,570 --> 00:43:33,775
"Whoever--
Whoever smells the--"

610
00:43:47,323 --> 00:43:51,427
I can't stop
rolling down the hill!

611
00:44:01,572 --> 00:44:04,141
Gale!Jennifer!

612
00:44:04,408 --> 00:44:06,144
- Dewey!
- Dewey!

613
00:44:06,377 --> 00:44:08,179
Dewey, where are you?

614
00:44:08,413 --> 00:44:12,017
Over here, Dewey!

615
00:44:13,752 --> 00:44:18,223
- Dewey!
- Gale!

616
00:44:18,390 --> 00:44:22,028
Gale, behind you!

617
00:44:30,870 --> 00:44:33,974
Dewey!
Are you all right?

618
00:44:34,208 --> 00:44:37,177
Yeah, never been better.

619
00:44:37,411 --> 00:44:39,714
Yeah, I'm all right.
Where'd he go?

620
00:44:39,947 --> 00:44:44,185
- He must've rolled under the car.
- All right, stay close.

621
00:44:51,493 --> 00:44:54,230
Is he back there?

622
00:44:54,463 --> 00:44:56,965
- No.
- No?

623
00:44:57,232 --> 00:45:01,538
He's fast.
Could've sworn I hit him.

624
00:45:04,574 --> 00:45:07,911
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

625
00:45:08,545 --> 00:45:10,113
Thanks for saving me.

626
00:45:10,380 --> 00:45:13,718
Ah, it's habit.

627
00:45:15,353 --> 00:45:18,756
Oh, God.

628
00:45:19,390 --> 00:45:23,228
What the fuck happened to you?

629
00:45:23,494 --> 00:45:25,697
-Jennifer, wait a minute.
- Who gave you a place to stay?

630
00:45:25,931 --> 00:45:29,101
-Who are you supposed to be protecting?
-Jennifer!

631
00:45:29,335 --> 00:45:33,139
Hey!

632
00:45:36,909 --> 00:45:40,513
My lawyer liked that.

633
00:45:40,714 --> 00:45:44,384
Not as much as I did.

634
00:45:48,756 --> 00:45:51,892
- Angelina?
- Tom was in the house.

635
00:45:52,093 --> 00:45:57,598
- How'd you end up way over there?
- Oh, my God! Tom was in the house!

636
00:45:59,434 --> 00:46:03,972
- Are we safe?
- Safe from who?

637
00:46:07,243 --> 00:46:10,713
Wait a second!

638
00:46:13,616 --> 00:46:17,186
Another picture.

639
00:46:20,858 --> 00:46:24,394
<i>Whoever it is is now taking credit
for Maureen Prescott's murder.</i>

640
00:46:24,661 --> 00:46:27,465
But we know who killed Maureen
Prescott. Billy Loomis and Stu Macher.

641
00:46:27,665 --> 00:46:29,801
-I mean, they even told Sidney
how they did it.
- Yeah, but if I'm not mistaken...

642
00:46:30,035 --> 00:46:32,036
you said in your book that
Sidney got it wrong once before.

643
00:46:32,303 --> 00:46:34,739
She accused Cotton Weary
of murdering her mother.

644
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:37,709
And he was sent away for it.
Maybe there is a third killer.

645
00:46:37,976 --> 00:46:39,845
Sidney might know something.

646
00:46:40,045 --> 00:46:42,315
I told you.
I don't know where Sidney is.

647
00:46:42,582 --> 00:46:44,883
And even if there was a third killer,
Sidney doesn't know about it.

648
00:46:45,117 --> 00:46:48,121
That is for me to decide.
I need to talk to her, Mr. Riley.
She is a key element in this case.

649
00:46:48,354 --> 00:46:50,356
I have a press conference in an hour.
I need to explain...

650
00:46:50,590 --> 00:46:52,792
why there are three dead celebrities
and a bodyguard.

651
00:46:53,026 --> 00:46:55,529
And a very angry mayor.

652
00:46:55,796 --> 00:46:57,497
Okay, look, we all know this has
something to do with Stab 3.

653
00:46:57,764 --> 00:47:00,501
But what we do not know is why
the killer keeps leaving pictures...

654
00:47:00,701 --> 00:47:02,837
of Maureen Prescott
taken over 25 years ago.

655
00:47:03,071 --> 00:47:05,539
And the photographs taken at the same
studio Stab 3 is shooting out of.

656
00:47:05,806 --> 00:47:07,208
What does this
have to do with Sid?

657
00:47:07,442 --> 00:47:09,912
Who knows more about Maureen
Prescott than her own daughter?

658
00:47:10,112 --> 00:47:13,515
Well, Sid's dad couldn't help you,
and he was married to Maureen.

659
00:47:13,749 --> 00:47:15,451
What's your problem?

660
00:47:15,684 --> 00:47:19,889
Last night you were almost charcoal.
You gonna help us or what?

661
00:47:20,122 --> 00:47:21,991
Do you wanna have this
conversation with a polygraph?

662
00:47:22,225 --> 00:47:27,397
- Is that a threat, Detective?
- When it's a threat, you'll know it.

663
00:47:27,631 --> 00:47:29,700
- Was that a threat?
- Boys, boys.

664
00:47:29,900 --> 00:47:32,102
Why don't we compare
our gun calibres later?

665
00:47:32,369 --> 00:47:35,406
- The issue is Maureen Prescott.
- Wrong. The issue is Sidney Prescott.

666
00:47:35,639 --> 00:47:39,210
And either Mr Riley is going
