- Let's go, let's go.

885
01:04:45,063 --> 01:04:47,533
I heard her voice.
I saw her, Dewey.

886
01:04:47,767 --> 01:04:50,570
- Upstairs. Come on, let's go.
- It's okay, Sid.

887
01:04:50,804 --> 01:04:52,839
You weren't supposed
to go in that house.

888
01:04:53,106 --> 01:04:54,941
It's all set up for the murder scene.

889
01:04:55,175 --> 01:04:56,944
- I'm sorry you had to see that.
- He was in there, Dewey.

890
01:04:57,177 --> 01:05:01,548
- He was in there, I swear, I swear.
- You know I believe you.

891
01:05:02,883 --> 01:05:05,652
- What happened?
- Kincaid, hey.

892
01:05:05,886 --> 01:05:09,023
There's nobody up here.

893
01:05:12,860 --> 01:05:16,465
Come on.

894
01:05:17,266 --> 01:05:19,768
- Come on.
- Okay, so I stole the mask.

895
01:05:20,002 --> 01:05:23,105
Whatever. I didn't know you got
the gas chamber for that.

896
01:05:23,339 --> 01:05:25,808
- You stole the mask?
- I took it.

897
01:05:26,041 --> 01:05:29,045
- You took the mask
or you stole the mask?
- I-I took it as like a souvenir.

898
01:05:29,279 --> 01:05:31,614
- Don't look at me. I didn't take shit.
- I know he was there.

899
01:05:31,848 --> 01:05:33,683
I am not dreaming,
I am not crazy.

900
01:05:33,950 --> 01:05:36,987
- He was there in Woodsboro.
- That's not Woodsboro, Sidney.

901
01:05:37,254 --> 01:05:41,659
You know what I mean. But he was there.
He or she, or whoever this is.

902
01:05:41,892 --> 01:05:44,328
We're gonna take you back
to the station, keep you under watch.

903
01:05:44,528 --> 01:05:46,831
Put you in a safe house.
Whatever it takes.

904
01:05:47,065 --> 01:05:50,402
Come on.

905
01:05:50,402 --> 01:05:52,971
It's all right, Sid.
We all believe you.

906
01:05:53,271 --> 01:05:56,742
- He's watching.
- And he wants you.

907
01:05:59,545 --> 01:06:01,314
- Hey, Dew.
- Dew.
- Come on.

908
01:06:01,514 --> 01:06:04,050
- We have to go catch up with Sid.
- Take a look at this first.

909
01:06:04,251 --> 01:06:06,152
- Someone we know?
- Where'd you get this?

910
01:06:06,386 --> 01:06:09,623
- We got it. Archives.
- Sidney's mother was an actress.
Three movies.

911
01:06:09,857 --> 01:06:14,228
-Horror movies.
-Wanna know who produced all three?
-Who?

912
01:06:14,461 --> 01:06:16,263
- There'll be other movies, Roman.
- Not only did they--

913
01:06:16,497 --> 01:06:19,300
did they kill the film,
but they killed my cast.

914
01:06:19,567 --> 01:06:22,537
Now, nobody's gonna wanna work
with me. Variety called me a pariah.

915
01:06:22,771 --> 01:06:26,140
I don't even know what a pariah is.
Why-Why couldn't someone
have killed the cast from Stab 1?

916
01:06:26,374 --> 01:06:28,677
Huh? Or Stab 2? Why me?
What--John, what did we do wrong?

917
01:06:28,911 --> 01:06:31,112
Hollywood is full of criminals
whose careers are flourishing.

918
01:06:31,346 --> 01:06:33,415
I'm not a criminal!
I was questioned.

919
01:06:33,715 --> 01:06:35,418
Yeah, but that's all.
I was questioned. That's it.

920
01:06:35,718 --> 01:06:38,420
- That's good foryour mystique.
- You think it will help me get work?

921
01:06:38,654 --> 01:06:40,556
Roman. John.

922
01:06:40,790 --> 01:06:43,593
Jennifer, and guests.
To what do I owe the honour?

923
01:06:43,794 --> 01:06:47,464
- Rina Reynolds.
- Rina Reynolds? Who's Rina Reynolds?

924
01:06:47,664 --> 01:06:51,034
Why don't you head to the house?
Tell everybody not to cut
the cake without me.

925
01:06:51,268 --> 01:06:53,470
- Oh, God, I forgot. Your birthday.
- Yeah.

926
01:06:53,704 --> 01:06:56,341
- Happy birthday, Roman.
- Yeah, as if life isn't tragic enough.

927
01:06:56,574 --> 01:07:01,112
Shut the doors behind you, please.

928
01:07:01,980 --> 01:07:04,183
So, you knew
Sidney Prescott's mother.

929
01:07:04,415 --> 01:07:07,452
- Who?
- Rina Reynolds?

930
01:07:07,753 --> 01:07:10,790
Do you know how many actors have
worked for me? Hundreds. Thousands.

931
01:07:11,022 --> 01:07:14,193
- He didn't say she was an actor.
- Good catch.

932
01:07:14,427 --> 01:07:16,596
- So what's the point?
- Uh, no point.

933
01:07:16,796 --> 01:07:19,499
I'm just gonna give, uh,
Detective Kincaid a call.

934
01:07:19,699 --> 01:07:23,303
I remember. She was a bit player
in a couple of my movies.

935
01:07:23,570 --> 01:07:25,906
- A nobody. So what does it matter?
- Oh, come on.

936
01:07:26,106 --> 01:07:29,543
You have made millions
off the story of her murder.

937
01:07:29,777 --> 01:07:32,513
You're obsessed with her,
and you're obsessed with her daughter!

938
01:07:32,713 --> 01:07:35,717
All right, easy, Geraldo.
Why don't you tell us the truth?

939
01:07:35,984 --> 01:07:39,821
What the hell are you guys getting at?
I make horror films, that's what I do.

940
01:07:40,055 --> 01:07:41,990
The studio came to me with Stab.

941
01:07:42,191 --> 01:07:44,826
They came to me.
Check it out.

942
01:07:45,026 --> 01:07:47,596
- But you knew who she was.
- When we did the first Stab...

943
01:07:47,796 --> 01:07:49,932
I realized I had known
Maureen Prescott before.

944
01:07:50,199 --> 01:07:52,401
I mean, as Rina.

945
01:07:52,601 --> 01:07:56,173
I couldn't tell anyone.
Can you imagine the press?

946
01:07:56,440 --> 01:07:58,708
And now?
I mean, murders on your set.

947
01:07:58,942 --> 01:08:01,144
- And-And still you say nothing?
- Get real.

948
01:08:01,445 --> 01:08:03,714
- That would make me a suspect.
-Just because you knew her?

949
01:08:03,915 --> 01:08:06,150
- Yeah.
- I don't think so.

950
01:08:06,383 --> 01:08:09,988
Just what did happen to Maureen
when she was in Hollywood?

951
01:08:10,722 --> 01:08:13,157
Now, you listen to me, Lois Lane.
Let it go. It's dead and buried.

952
01:08:13,391 --> 01:08:16,495
How would you like to see it
dug up on national TV?

953
01:08:16,762 --> 01:08:20,098
Why don't you tell me
what happened?

954
01:08:21,266 --> 01:08:24,337
It was in the '70s.
Everything was different.

955
01:08:24,536 --> 01:08:28,141
I was well-known for my parties.
Rina knew what they were.

956
01:08:28,341 --> 01:08:32,545
It was for girls like her to meet men.
Men who could get them parts...

957
01:08:32,779 --> 01:08:34,548
if they made
the right impression.

958
01:08:34,748 --> 01:08:36,817
Nothing happened to her
that she didn't invite...

959
01:08:37,117 --> 01:08:40,187
in one way or another
no matter what she said afterwards.

960
01:08:40,387 --> 01:08:43,424
- Are you saying she--
- I'm saying things got out of hand.

961
01:08:43,725 --> 01:08:47,428
Maybe they did take advantage of her.
You know, Maybe the sad truth is...

962
01:08:47,662 --> 01:08:51,033
this is not the city
for innocents.

963
01:08:51,299 --> 01:08:54,102
No charges were brought.
And the bottom line is...

964
01:08:54,369 --> 01:08:56,739
Rina Reynolds
wouldn't play by the rules.

965
01:08:57,039 --> 01:08:59,107
You wanna get ahead in Hollywood?

966
01:08:59,308 --> 01:09:03,980
You gotta play the game, or go home.

967
01:09:08,451 --> 01:09:10,821
What do you know
about trilogies?

968
01:09:11,120 --> 01:09:14,324
- You mean, like movie trilogies?
- You seem to like movies, Detective.

969
01:09:14,558 --> 01:09:18,762
Call me Mark, would you? 'Cause
I'm gonna keep calling you Sidney.

970
01:09:18,962 --> 01:09:22,667
I'll call you Mark when
you catch the killer, Detective.

971
01:09:23,401 --> 01:09:27,272
All I know about movie trilogies
is that in the third one...

972
01:09:27,472 --> 01:09:31,142
all bets are off.

973
01:09:31,209 --> 01:09:33,111
- Did you request this case?
- No. They tend to put me...

974
01:09:33,345 --> 01:09:35,114
on the ones that deal
with the business.

975
01:09:35,347 --> 01:09:38,350
I grew up here,
and I know my way around the studios.

976
01:09:38,584 --> 01:09:40,686
Huh.

977
01:09:40,920 --> 01:09:44,191
Must be exciting.
Beautiful place, beautiful people.

978
01:09:44,391 --> 01:09:48,028
To me, Hollywood is about death.

979
01:09:48,495 --> 01:09:50,965
Excuse me?

980
01:09:51,164 --> 01:09:54,401
I'm a homicide detective, remember?

981
01:09:54,635 --> 01:09:57,238
And when you see what I see
day in and day out...

982
01:09:57,472 --> 01:09:59,774
the violence
that people do to each other...

983
01:10:00,041 --> 01:10:01,776
you get haunted.

984
01:10:02,043 --> 01:10:05,346
I think you know about that.

985
01:10:06,081 --> 01:10:08,217
What do you mean?

986
01:10:08,484 --> 01:10:11,353
I know what it's like
to see ghosts that don't go away.

987
01:10:11,586 --> 01:10:16,626
To be watching a scary movie in
your head, whether you want to or not.

988
01:10:16,960 --> 01:10:21,531
Watching it alone.

989
01:10:22,365 --> 01:10:24,801
Ghosts are tough.
You can't shoot ghosts.

990
01:10:25,001 --> 01:10:27,671
Can't arrest ghosts.

991
01:10:27,938 --> 01:10:31,241
But the best way to stop being
haunted is to be with people.

992
01:10:31,441 --> 01:10:33,277
You're here, you're not hiding.

993
01:10:33,511 --> 01:10:38,282
You've done the right thing,
Miss Prescott.

994
01:10:41,152 --> 01:10:44,856
What did you know about your mother?

995
01:10:47,860 --> 01:10:50,296
I always thought
I had the perfect mom.

996
01:10:50,530 --> 01:10:53,933
Perfect family.

997
01:10:54,834 --> 01:10:59,639
Till I found out I was wrong.
She, um--

998
01:11:00,874 --> 01:11:05,646
She had a secret life, and I tried
to understand that, and, um...

999
01:11:05,879 --> 01:11:11,318
soon as I thought that I had,
more secrets.

1000
01:11:13,421 --> 01:11:16,191
I don't know who my mom was.

1001
01:11:16,491 --> 01:11:20,162
You know who she was to you.

1002
01:11:23,099 --> 01:11:24,967
Here's the deal.
I'm off to search the set.

1003
01:11:25,167 --> 01:11:29,138
I think what you saw is real.
That's the good news.

1004
01:11:29,372 --> 01:11:31,407
- How is that good news?
- Because that means...

1005
01:11:31,607 --> 01:11:34,444
that we're dealing with
an ordinary flesh-and-blood killer.

1006
01:11:34,678 --> 01:11:38,014
- And I know how
to handle guys like that.
- Oh, yeah? How?

1007
01:11:38,214 --> 01:11:42,486
Catch him or kill him.

1008
01:11:44,455 --> 01:11:48,226
Hey, Detective.

1009
01:11:48,493 --> 01:11:52,297
What's your favourite
scary movie?

1010
01:11:54,499 --> 01:11:57,902
My life.

1011
01:11:59,304 --> 01:12:01,741
Mine too.

1012
01:12:02,475 --> 01:12:04,244
We have to think.
Strategize.

1013
01:12:04,477 --> 01:12:07,146
- Milton's the key to everything.
- He's a pervert, he's not a killer.

1014
01:12:07,380 --> 01:12:09,983
He's gotta be involved somehow.
We should follow him.

1015
01:12:10,217 --> 01:12:12,018
We're gonna go back to the precinct and
we're gonna tell Kincaid and Sidney...

1016
01:12:12,218 --> 01:12:14,187
what we found out.

1017
01:12:14,421 --> 01:12:17,658
My Gale would be much more aggressive.
My Gale would suspect everybody.

1018
01:12:17,858 --> 01:12:21,462
- My Gale would--
- Shut up!
- Shut up!

1019
01:12:22,997 --> 01:12:25,466
<i>- Riley here.
- Dewey, it's Sidney.
- Hey, Sid.</i>

1020
01:12:25,700 --> 01:12:27,535
<i>- I'm with Gale.
We're on our way to see you.
- No.</i>

1021
01:12:27,769 --> 01:12:30,973
<i>Listen, I'm not at the station.
John Milton called me and said
he had something to tell me.</i>

1022
01:12:31,206 --> 01:12:33,408
<i>Something about my mom.
I'm going to meet him at his house.</i>

1023
01:12:33,642 --> 01:12:35,745
Wait, Sid, I'm not so sure
that's a good idea.

1024
01:12:35,978 --> 01:12:38,680
<i>It's okay. Kincaid's with me.
I've got official big-time...</i>

1025
01:12:38,947 --> 01:12:42,085
<i>L.A.P.D. protection, but
I'd feel better if you were there.</i>

1026
01:12:42,285 --> 01:12:46,222
<i>- We're on our way, but still, Sid--
- Thanks.</i>

1027
01:12:46,456 --> 01:12:51,528
- What?
- Looks like we're going
to that party after all.

1028
01:13:00,571 --> 01:13:03,175
Hey, guys. Come on in.
Join the party.

1029
01:13:03,408 --> 01:13:05,209
Yeah, well, actually,
we're here to see Sidney.

1030
01:13:05,443 --> 01:13:07,412
- Really? Sidney's here.
- Where?

1031
01:13:07,646 --> 01:13:10,683
- Where's Sidney?
- She's right there!

1032
01:13:10,950 --> 01:13:14,086
Jesus!
Not "Sidney," Sidney.

1033
01:13:14,353 --> 01:13:17,590
- Like I'm "Gale" and she's Gale.
- Sidney Prescott?

1034
01:13:17,824 --> 01:13:20,426
- Yeah.
- No, I'd never invite her here.

1035
01:13:20,660 --> 01:13:24,098
- She's on her way.
- Well, the more the merrier.

1036
01:13:24,331 --> 01:13:27,901
God, this house is incredible.

1037
01:13:28,135 --> 01:13:30,905
-It's old Hollywood.
-Yeah. Could the dude have more money?

1038
01:13:31,139 --> 01:13:33,908
Supposedly, Milton has
a secret screening room...

1039
01:13:34,141 --> 01:13:35,910
that was like the scene
back in the '70s, you know.

1040
01:13:36,144 --> 01:13:40,114
It was, like, drinks and drugs
and girls and movies and shit.

1041
01:13:40,348 --> 01:13:42,885
Wow! Wish I could've seen it.

1042
01:13:43,152 --> 01:13:44,953
Big old screening room
shouldn't be too hard to find.

1043
01:13:45,153 --> 01:13:46,955
I'm gonna go--
I'm gonna go check this place out.

1044
01:13:47,189 --> 01:13:50,426
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Just one damn minute.
There's a psycho killer on the loose.

1045
01:13:50,660 --> 01:13:53,029
And you want to go traipsing around
this gigantic mansion?

1046
01:13:53,262 --> 01:13:55,498
Have you ever actually seen
the Stab movies? Every time...

1047
01:13:55,732 --> 01:13:58,167
this dude enters a room,
he ends up a goddam shish kebab.

1048
01:13:58,434 --> 01:14:01,304
- I'll go with you, Roman.
- There you go. You guys wanna come?

1049
01:14:01,538 --> 01:14:05,308
It'll be okay.
We're gonna stick together.

1050
01:14:05,542 --> 01:14:08,913
-You're not stickin'. Wait up.
-We're gonna stay here and wait for Sid.

1051
01:14:09,147 --> 01:14:12,149
We'll be right back!

1052
01:14:12,383 --> 01:14:15,253
If-If you were a screening room...

1053
01:14:15,553 --> 01:14:18,890
where would you be?

1054
01:14:20,158 --> 01:14:23,496
I bet in the basement.

1055
01:14:24,629 --> 01:14:28,468
I don't like basements.

1056
01:14:30,837 --> 01:14:34,174
Ooh, it's spooky.

1057
01:14:44,852 --> 01:14:46,754
- Ooh, Weredad.
- Damn, it's dark in here.

1058
01:14:46,988 --> 01:14:49,424
- I loved that movie.
- Forget the movie!
What if Milton's crazy...

1059
01:14:49,658 --> 01:14:52,026
and he's gonna jump outta his screening
room with a sling blade or something?

1060
01:14:52,293 --> 01:14:55,664
- He won't.
- You sure about that?

1061
01:14:59,835 --> 01:15:03,139
- What's down there?
- Zombies and aliens.

1062
01:15:03,339 --> 01:15:05,708
You know, what you look like
without make-up, Jennifer.

1063
01:15:05,941 --> 01:15:08,912
Jesus. Stop pretending
I wasn't the best you've ever had.

1064
01:15:09,179 --> 01:15:14,518
- Oh, stop pretending I even remember.
- Stop pretending!

1065
01:15:18,054 --> 01:15:21,359
Roman?

1066
01:15:31,402 --> 01:15:34,740
Roman?

1067
01:15:37,977 --> 01:15:41,180
- Any sign of her?
- No.

1068
01:15:41,447 --> 01:15:43,583
This is so strange.

1069
01:15:43,783 --> 01:15:45,551
It sure is.

1070
01:15:45,818 --> 01:15:47,754
Dewey, do you have caller I.D.
on your cell phone?

1071
01:15:47,988 --> 01:15:51,524
-Yeah.
-All right, use it and-and press "send."

1072
01:16:00,001 --> 01:16:03,338
What the hell?

1073
01:16:12,948 --> 01:16:16,786
What is this thing?

1074
01:16:17,420 --> 01:16:21,391
Is this what he--
What the hell?

1075
01:16:22,959 --> 01:16:25,128
Dewey, he's got our voices.

1076
01:16:25,395 --> 01:16:27,130
He's got Sid.

1077
01:16:27,397 --> 01:16:29,166
He's got us all.

1078
01:16:29,400 --> 01:16:32,970
- Oh, my God. We gotta find her.
- Come on.

1079
01:16:33,203 --> 01:16:35,440
All right, take the gun.

1080
01:16:35,673 --> 01:16:37,843
Go find Roman and Jennifer.
I'm gonna get the others.

1081
01:16:38,075 --> 01:16:41,446
- Be careful.
- You too.

1082
01:16:42,547 --> 01:16:48,087
Tyson! Angelina!
You up there?

1083
01:16:48,888 --> 01:16:51,557
- Roman!
- Tyson!

1084
01:16:51,824 --> 01:16:53,960
Angelina!

1085
01:16:54,160 --> 01:16:56,963
Damn it!

1086
01:16:57,164 --> 01:16:58,998
Okay, come on.
We gotta get out of here.

1087
01:16:59,232 --> 01:17:01,268
- Where's Angelina?
- I don't know. She went in here.

1088
01:17:01,535 --> 01:17:03,470
- I came in after her. Now she's gone.
- Great.

1089
01:17:03,671 --> 01:17:08,275
- What's wrong?
- Looks like Stab 3
is back in production.

1090
01:17:09,877 --> 01:17:13,014
Roman!

1091
01:17:13,247 --> 01:17:17,152
Jennifer!

1092
01:17:26,895 --> 01:17:30,734
Jennifer!

1093
01:17:34,337 --> 01:17:37,207
Roman!

1094
01:17:37,441 --> 01:17:40,811
Jennifer!

1095
01:17:47,518 --> 01:17:51,756
Roman?

1096
01:18:06,038 --> 01:18:07,807
- Is he dead?
- Yeah, very.

1097
01:18:08,041 --> 01:18:12,011
Dewey! Dewey!

1098
01:18:15,315 --> 01:18:18,085
Dewey?

1099
01:18:18,318 --> 01:18:20,721
Dewey!

1100
01:18:20,921 --> 01:18:23,057
God, I'm sorry.
Jennifer, Gale, look.

1101
01:18:23,324 --> 01:18:25,659
- I found a secret passage.
- Roman's dead.

1102
01:18:25,893 --> 01:18:28,263
- What?
- The killer's here.
- What?
- Come on.

1103
01:18:28,496 --> 01:18:31,833
- Let go of me! I'm getting out of here!
- You're not safe alone!

1104
01:18:32,033 --> 01:18:33,835
Listen to me!

1105
01:18:34,036 --> 01:18:37,974
I did not fuck that pig Milton
to get a leading role...

1106
01:18:38,206 --> 01:18:43,446
just to die here with second-rate
celebrities like you two!

1107
01:18:45,314 --> 01:18:48,385
- Gale! I'm up here.
- Come on.

1108
01:18:48,652 --> 01:18:51,888
- Dewey!
- You guys should get out too.

1109
01:18:52,122 --> 01:18:55,960
It's crazy to still be here.

1110
01:19:00,998 --> 01:19:05,336
- Wait!
- Come on!

1111
01:19:19,251 --> 01:19:22,055
- Dewey!
- Gale, Jennifer, up here!

1112
01:19:22,288 --> 01:19:24,891
Dewey, here.
He got Roman and Angelina too.

1113
01:19:25,124 --> 01:19:28,829
- We'll be safer if we
stick together, won't we?
- Of course. Why--

1114
01:19:30,865 --> 01:19:32,566
What's goin' on?
Oh, shit!

1115
01:19:32,800 --> 01:19:36,004
- Hey!
- Dewey!

1116
01:19:36,037 --> 01:19:38,839
Dewey!

1117
01:19:39,106 --> 01:19:42,410
No!

1118
01:19:50,720 --> 01:19:53,823
Help! Police!
Help! Help!

1119
01:19:54,056 --> 01:19:58,095
Police! Help!

1120
01:20:04,401 --> 01:20:07,905
Oh, you motherfucker!

1121
01:20:43,344 --> 01:20:46,714
Damn!

1122
01:20:49,417 --> 01:20:54,089
Dewey! Dewey!

1123
01:20:56,258 --> 01:21:00,262
Behind the mirror, Dewey!

1124
01:21:00,996 --> 01:21:03,232
Gale! Get away! Dewey!

1125
01:21:03,466 --> 01:21:05,534
- Do you hear something?
- Get away from me, you asshole.

1126
01:21:05,768 --> 01:21:10,273
- Get away from me! You don't scare me!
- Look, Gale. The mirror's moving.

1127
01:21:10,507 --> 01:21:13,710
- Gale! Gale!
- Stand back, Gale.

1128
01:21:13,944 --> 01:21:16,947
You can't kill me. I'm the killer
in Stab 3. I'm the killer!

1129
01:21:17,181 --> 01:21:21,252
Gale, cover!

1130
01:21:21,819 --> 01:21:25,256
Dewey!

1131
01:21:34,132 --> 01:21:36,368
- Tyson!
- Tyson!

1132
01:21:36,635 --> 01:21:38,370
I'm gonna check down here.
You call for help.

1133
01:21:38,637 --> 01:21:40,739
Okay.

1134
01:21:40,973 --> 01:21:43,910
Tyson!

1135
01:21:44,144 --> 01:21:47,514
- Tyson?
- Any sign of him?

1136
01:21:47,747 --> 01:21:51,185
- No.
- All right. I'm gonna check out front.

1137
01:21:56,657 --> 01:22:00,027
Dew--

1138
01:22:22,819 --> 01:22:26,189
Gale!

1139
01:22:27,023 --> 01:22:30,795
Gale!

1140
01:22:31,395 --> 01:22:33,664
Gale!

1141
01:22:33,898 --> 01:22:37,736
- Dewey?
- Gale!

1142
01:22:39,070 --> 01:22:42,440
Gale!

1143
01:22:45,877 --> 01:22:48,280
<i>- Who is this?
- Dewey, it's me.</i>

1144
01:22:48,514 --> 01:22:51,284
Gale, where are you?

1145
01:22:51,517 --> 01:22:53,786
<i>I'm in the basement.
I'm trapped.</i>

1146
01:22:54,019 --> 01:22:57,624
<i>- Where?
- There's a door in the kitchen.</i>

1147
01:22:58,624 --> 01:23:02,028
<i>Hurry.</i>

1148
01:23:04,098 --> 01:23:07,901
Wait. How do I know this is
you, Gale, and not the killer?

1149
01:23:08,168 --> 01:23:11,339
<i>Dewey, open the fucking door.
It's me.</i>

1150
01:23:11,638 --> 01:23:14,141
Well, don't you think that's
what the killer would say?

1151
01:23:14,442 --> 01:23:20,582
<i>Come on. He's out cold
at the bottom of the stairs.</i>

1152
01:23:21,283 --> 01:23:24,787
Hey!

1153
01:23:35,765 --> 01:23:39,636
Dewey. Dewey.

1154
01:23:48,446 --> 01:23:50,248
All right, all right.
It's pizza, not a party.

1155
01:23:50,482 --> 01:23:54,686
Everybody get back to work.
Anybody seen my fuckin' partner?

1156
01:23:54,953 --> 01:23:58,324
Hey, Morgan,
what did you pay?

1157
01:24:44,240 --> 01:24:47,243
<i>- Hello?
- Hello?</i>

1158
01:24:47,477 --> 01:24:49,846
<i>- Who is this?
- Who is this?</i>

1159
01:24:50,080 --> 01:24:54,918
<i>- Um, w-who's calling?
- Um, w-who's calling?</i>

1160
01:24:55,219 --> 01:25:00,257
Gale, Dewey, whoever, um, call me back.
I can only hear myself.

1161
01:25:00,458 --> 01:25:04,830
<i>I only hear you too, Sidney.</i>

1162
01:25:04,997 --> 01:25:08,133
<i>- Who is this?
- The question isn't who I am.</i>

1163
01:25:08,400 --> 01:25:11,936
<i>The question is:
Who's with me?</i>

1164
01:25:12,203 --> 01:25:13,939
<i>- Sidney, stay away!
- Sidney!</i>

1165
01:25:14,206 --> 01:25:17,377
<i>Don't do it. If you do one thing
to attract attention to yourself...</i>

1166
01:25:17,610 --> 01:25:20,212
<i>one thing,
I'll kill them both.</i>

1167
01:25:20,413 --> 01:25:25,685
<i>Now, do you have somewhere
we can be alone?</i>

1168
01:25:25,885 --> 01:25:29,990
<i>- Yes.
- Yeah. Go there.</i>

1169
01:25:35,129 --> 01:25:37,699
<i>Oh, it's hard being friends
with you, Sidney.</i>

1170
01:25:37,932 --> 01:25:40,768
<i>When you're friends with Sidney,
you die.</i>

1171
01:25:40,969 --> 01:25:45,073
<i>Well, these friends don't have to,
Sidney. It's up to you.</i>

1172
01:25:45,373 --> 01:25:47,209
<i>- How do I know their voices are--
- Are real?</i>

1173
01:25:47,442 --> 01:25:49,278
<i>How do you know
you're not hearing things?</i>

1174
01:25:49,478 --> 01:25:54,417
<i>How do you know I'm not someone
in your head? Somewhere you know.</i>

1175
01:25:54,684 --> 01:25:56,920
<i>- Don't come here, Sidney!
- Dewey!</i>

1176
01:25:57,153 --> 01:26:00,123
<i>- Or do you?
- You're dead.</i>

1177
01:26:00,423 --> 01:26:02,526
<i>I don't want them.
I want you.</i>

1178
01:26:02,759 --> 01:26:05,295
<i>It's simple.
You show yourself, they survive.</i>

1179
01:26:05,495 --> 01:26:07,798
<i>- You run, they die.
- Oh, God!</i>

1180
01:26:08,065 --> 01:26:11,768
<i>Don't you wanna know, Sidney,
who killed her?</i>

1181
01:26:11,969 --> 01:26:15,173
<i>Don't you wanna know
who killed your mother?</i>

1182
01:26:15,440 --> 01:26:17,209
- Have you seen Kincaid?
- Yeah, I saw him go out.

1183
01:26:17,442 --> 01:26:19,010
- Wallace is still lookin' for him.
- Where?

1184
01:26:19,277 --> 01:26:23,082
<i>She'd have been so happy, Sidney,
to know we'd be together.</i>

1185
01:26:23,282 --> 01:26:28,387
<i>- Where?
- I'll call you when you're on your way.</i>

1186
01:26:30,723 --> 01:26:34,761
Shit. Shit. Shit.

1187
01:27:39,264 --> 01:27:43,169
Holy shit.

1188
01:27:51,011 --> 01:27:53,213
<i>- What?
- You follow directions well, Sidney.</i>

1189
01:27:53,513 --> 01:27:55,416
<i>Now, welcome to the final act.</i>

1190
01:27:55,649 --> 01:27:58,186
<i>See that metal detector?</i>

1191
01:27:58,386 --> 01:28:02,156
<i>Use it.</i>

1192
01:28:04,860 --> 01:28:09,231
<i>All over, Sidney.
Everywhere.</i>

1193
01:28:12,300 --> 01:28:17,340
<i>Everywhere.
The other leg too.</i>

1194
01:28:19,975 --> 01:28:23,546
<i>Show it to me.</i>

1195
01:28:27,417 --> 01:28:30,788
<i>Throw it in the pool.</i>

1196
01:28:32,422 --> 01:28:34,191
<i>Now, come inside, Sidney.</i>

1197
01:28:34,425 --> 01:28:37,095
No fucking way. How do I know
they're not dead already?

1198
01:28:37,328 --> 01:28:40,465
<i>They're right inside,
waiting for you.</i>

1199
01:28:40,665 --> 01:28:44,036
<i>Look for yourself.</i>

1200
01:28:53,712 --> 01:28:58,518
<i>Now that we're all here,
the party can begin.</i>

1201
01:28:58,751 --> 01:29:01,855
- Dewey.
- Sid.

1202
01:29:02,155 --> 01:29:04,858
- Where is he?
- I don't know.

1203
01:29:05,092 --> 01:29:08,862
He's right there!

1204
01:29:13,267 --> 01:29:15,803
Oh, shit.

1205
01:29:16,037 --> 01:29:17,639
Think again.

1206
01:29:17,873 --> 01:29:21,643
It's your turn to scream, asshole.

1207
01:29:23,412 --> 01:29:27,616
Yeah!

1208
01:29:30,586 --> 01:29:33,789
- It's okay.Just give me a second.
- Okay.

1209
01:29:34,023 --> 01:29:38,861
- Hurry, Sid.
- Sidney? Sidney?

1210
01:29:40,096 --> 01:29:43,868
Where is he?

1211
01:29:45,535 --> 01:29:49,006
Be careful!

1212
01:29:54,479 --> 01:29:57,749
I heard shots. Tyson's dead.
What's goin' on?

1213
01:29:57,983 --> 01:30:00,418
- What're you doin' here, Kincaid?
- Lookin' for you.

1214
01:30:00,685 --> 01:30:03,556
Tyson said there was a party here
tonight, and I thought, uh-oh.

1215
01:30:03,789 --> 01:30:05,624
Third act celebration.
Thought I better check it out.

1216
01:30:05,858 --> 01:30:09,629
Alone?
Where's your partner?

1217
01:30:11,898 --> 01:30:14,567
Hey, Miss Prescott.

1218
01:30:14,834 --> 01:30:19,339
I'm here to help.
Put the gun down.

1219
01:30:20,240 --> 01:30:23,511
Put the gun down.

1220
01:30:26,180 --> 01:30:30,118
No!

1221
01:30:33,488 --> 01:30:37,726
Sid! Wake up, Sid!
Sid, come on!

1222
01:30:37,960 --> 01:30:41,664
- Wake up!
- Sidney!

1223
01:30:41,864 --> 01:30:44,100
Sid, shoot him! Sid!

1224
01:30:44,367 --> 01:30:47,904
Shoot the fucker!

1225
01:30:48,171 --> 01:30:52,342
Shoot him!

1226
01:30:55,412 --> 01:30:58,249
You want me, motherfucker?
Come and get me.

1227
01:30:58,483 --> 01:31:02,553
Run!

1228
01:31:47,202 --> 01:31:50,039
Sid.

1229
01:31:50,272 --> 01:31:53,475
Sid.

1230
01:31:53,776 --> 01:31:59,081
Come in here, please.

1231
01:31:59,916 --> 01:32:03,720
It's just me, Sid.

1232
01:32:03,987 --> 01:32:07,524
Oh, I was so pretty.

1233
01:32:07,791 --> 01:32:10,928
Everybody loved me.

1234
01:32:11,162 --> 01:32:15,433
Have you missed me, Sidney?

1235
01:32:15,967 --> 01:32:21,439
Would you like to hold me
one last time?

1236
01:32:21,740 --> 01:32:24,376
What's the matter?
What are you staring at?

1237
01:32:24,610 --> 01:32:30,416
Don't you remember your mother?

1238
01:32:39,893 --> 01:32:41,795
You're not going anywhere, Sidney.

1239
01:32:42,062 --> 01:32:47,635
It's time you came to terms
with me and with Mother.

1240
01:32:48,569 --> 01:32:51,206
Maybe you never
knew her at all, Sidney.

1241
01:32:51,439 --> 01:32:56,211
Maybe you just can't get past
the surface of things.

1242
01:32:56,411 --> 01:32:59,981
- Who the hell are you?
- The other half of you.

1243
01:33:00,181 --> 01:33:03,919
I searched for a mother too,
an actress named Rina Reynolds.

1244
01:33:04,153 --> 01:33:05,954
Tried to find her my whole life.

1245
01:33:06,255 --> 01:33:08,891
And four years ago,
I actually tracked her down.

1246
01:33:09,158 --> 01:33:12,161
Knocked at her door, thinking
she'd welcome me with open arms.

1247
01:33:12,361 --> 01:33:16,600
But she had a new life
and a new name: Maureen Prescott.

1248
01:33:16,833 --> 01:33:18,636
You were the only child
she claimed, Sidney.

1249
01:33:18,902 --> 01:33:21,605
She shut me out
in the cold forever.

1250
01:33:21,805 --> 01:33:25,743
Her own son.

1251
01:33:29,881 --> 01:33:34,519
Roman Bridger, director.
And brother.

1252
01:33:34,786 --> 01:33:37,156
She slammed the door in my face, Sid.
She said I was Rina's child...

1253
01:33:37,456 --> 01:33:39,458
and Rina was dead.

1254
01:33:39,658 --> 01:33:41,493
And it struck me.

1255
01:33:41,727 --> 01:33:44,798
What a good idea!
So I watched her.

1256
01:33:45,065 --> 01:33:48,768
I made a little home movie.
A little-little family film.

1257
01:33:49,002 --> 01:33:51,805
It seems Maureen--
Mom--

1258
01:33:52,005 --> 01:33:55,809
She really got around.
I mean, Cotton was one thing.

1259
01:33:56,076 --> 01:33:58,045
Everybody knew about that.

1260
01:33:58,279 --> 01:34:02,617
But Billy's father?
That was the key.

1261
01:34:02,884 --> 01:34:04,786
Your boyfriend didn't like seeing
his daddy in my film too much.

1262
01:34:04,986 --> 01:34:07,021
He didn't like it at all.

1263
01:34:07,255 --> 01:34:11,260
But once I supplied the motivation,
all the kid needed was a few pointers.

1264
01:34:11,493 --> 01:34:14,529
Have a partner to sell out in case
you get caught, find someone to frame.

1265
01:34:14,763 --> 01:34:16,999
It was like
he was making a movie.

1266
01:34:17,199 --> 01:34:21,571
You. This is all because ofyou.

1267
01:34:21,804 --> 01:34:25,042
I'm a director, Sid.

1268
01:34:25,342 --> 01:34:27,510
- I direct.
- Oh.

1269
01:34:27,710 --> 01:34:32,382
I had no idea that they were
gonna make a film of their own.

1270
01:34:33,216 --> 01:34:36,787
- Oh, shit.
- What a film it turned out to be, huh?

1271
01:34:36,988 --> 01:34:39,690
I mean, introducing Sidney,
the victim.

1272
01:34:39,890 --> 01:34:44,663
Sidney, the survivor.
Sidney, the star!

1273
01:34:58,411 --> 01:35:00,413
All right. You're gonna be all right.
Just apply pressure.

1274
01:35:00,613 --> 01:35:02,782
Here, take this.
Get the son ofa bitch.

1275
01:35:03,049 --> 01:35:04,451
Let's go.

1276
01:35:04,685 --> 01:35:07,420
Fine, you got what you wanted,
hero and villain face-to-face.

1277
01:35:07,654 --> 01:35:10,224
- Well, you know what happens now?
The villain dies!
- Exactly!

1278
01:35:10,458 --> 01:35:14,595
But I'm not the villain, Sid.
You are.

1279
01:35:14,795 --> 01:35:19,066
Here he is, the man who gave away
your mother's innocence.

1280
01:35:19,300 --> 01:35:21,503
Huh? What he did
to her made her a slut.

1281
01:35:21,736 --> 01:35:25,807
Didn't it? Huh? She never recovered from
that night, right here in this room.

1282
01:35:26,007 --> 01:35:29,345
They fucked her three ways from Sunday.
Ruined her life.

1283
01:35:29,612 --> 01:35:31,180
Ruined yours too,
didn't it, Sid?

1284
01:35:31,447 --> 01:35:33,716
You hate him, Sid?

1285
01:35:33,949 --> 01:35:39,288
Come on, I know you do.
I'm sure you do.

1286
01:35:39,489 --> 01:35:41,792
<i>I know who you are.
I know what happened to my mother.</i>

1287
01:35:41,992 --> 01:35:44,695
<i>And I want you to understand,
I'm gonna make you pay!</i>

1288
01:35:44,895 --> 01:35:46,663
That's what the police are gonna
find on Milton's answering machine...

1289
01:35:46,897 --> 01:35:50,334
right next to his lifeless,
mutilated corpse.

1290
01:35:50,535 --> 01:35:52,570
- What? Can't hear ya.
- You don't have to do this, Roman.

1291
01:35:52,837 --> 01:35:54,639
Just tell me what you want.
I can make it happen.

1292
01:35:54,906 --> 01:35:56,741
Any picture.
Name your budget. Script approval.

1293
01:35:56,942 --> 01:35:58,943
- Final cut!
- I already have it.

1294
01:35:59,177 --> 01:36:02,414
No!

1295
01:36:03,048 --> 01:36:04,817
God! You spineless bastard!

1296
01:36:05,051 --> 01:36:07,786
No, Sid, that would be you.
You did it all.

1297
01:36:08,053 --> 01:36:11,825
You did it, you called them all.
Even your closest friends.

1298
01:36:12,025 --> 01:36:14,294
Living in total isolation, the pressure
ofanother movie about you...

1299
01:36:14,561 --> 01:36:17,464
the discovery that Milton
destroyed Mommy dearest...

1300
01:36:17,664 --> 01:36:20,634
you finally just snapped!

1301
01:36:20,867 --> 01:36:25,106
One, two, three!

1302
01:36:26,106 --> 01:36:29,577
And who's our hero, huh?
The sole survivor. Who's the one...

1303
01:36:29,878 --> 01:36:33,514
who bravely faced down the psychopath
and killed her with her own knife?

1304
01:36:33,715 --> 01:36:35,817
You're gonna pay for the life
you stole from me, Sid.

1305
01:36:36,051 --> 01:36:39,621
For the mother, and for the family,
and for the stardom and--

1306
01:36:39,855 --> 01:36:41,957
Goddam it! Everything you have
that should've been mine!

1307
01:36:42,158 --> 01:36:45,028
God! Why don't you stop your whining
and get on with it?
I've heard this shit before!

1308
01:36:45,261 --> 01:36:47,396
- Stop!
- You know why you kill people,
Roman? Do you?

1309
01:36:47,663 --> 01:36:50,500
- I don't wanna hear it!
- Because you choose to!
There is no one else to blame!

1310
01:36:50,700 --> 01:36:53,803
- Stop it! Fucking damn it!
- Why don't you take
some fucking responsibility?

1311
01:36:54,037 --> 01:36:57,708
- Fuck you!
- Fuck you!

1312
01:37:08,953 --> 01:37:12,323
Sid? Sidney?

1313
01:37:19,498 --> 01:37:22,869
Sidney?

1314
01:37:29,643 --> 01:37:32,579
Sidney!

1315
01:37:44,760 --> 01:37:47,562
Sidney!

1316
01:37:49,631 --> 01:37:52,601
Leave her alone!

1317
01:38:02,045 --> 01:38:05,082
Dewey, do something!

1318
01:38:07,951 --> 01:38:12,322
- Stand back!
- Dewey!

1319
01:38:15,359 --> 01:38:19,029
Sid! Sid.

1320
01:38:41,388 --> 01:38:45,159
Sid?

1321
01:38:47,427 --> 01:38:51,032
Where is he?

1322
01:39:03,278 --> 01:39:06,415
Hey. Lose something?

1323
01:39:06,648 --> 01:39:09,786
Found something.

1324
01:39:30,408 --> 01:39:34,846
There's gotta be another way in there!
Come on!

1325
01:39:39,484 --> 01:39:43,990
You hurt her,
I swear I'll kill you!

1326
01:39:56,069 --> 01:40:00,173
-Dewey!
-Down this way. There's another hallway.

1327
01:40:10,485 --> 01:40:13,822
There's another door down here.

1328
01:40:19,361 --> 01:40:21,564
- This thing's not budging.
- Look around for something heavy.

1329
01:40:21,797 --> 01:40:25,801
- Go that way.
- Okay!

1330
01:40:49,361 --> 01:40:52,898
I shot you.

1331
01:40:56,435 --> 01:41:00,840
I guess we think alike.

1332
01:41:00,840 --> 01:41:03,543
Mother's dead.

1333
01:41:03,743 --> 01:41:07,147
And there is nothing
you can do about that.

1334
01:41:07,280 --> 01:41:10,317
I still got
to make my movie.

1335
01:41:10,618 --> 01:41:14,455
Stab 3, right?

1336
01:41:29,939 --> 01:41:33,709
Kincaid, hang in there.

1337
01:41:33,842 --> 01:41:38,815
Roman? It was Roman?

1338
